Package: perturbdyngen
Type: Package
Title: Paired Perturb-seq Simulation of Gene Regulatory Networks
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Weizhou", "Qian", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "78060663+cyclopenta@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Simulates knockdown (CRISPRi) and activation (CRISPRa) Perturb-seq
    screens on dyngen gene regulatory network models. Wild-type and perturbed cells
    are simulated as coupled pairs with common random numbers, so genes upstream of a
    perturbation are unchanged by construction. A guide UMI layer and an RNA capture
    layer (shared library size, negative binomial counts) turn molecule counts into
    Perturb-seq-like observations. Includes a network sampler (log-normal degrees,
    burn-in scaffolding, reachability repair), experiment designs, the networks and
    configuration files of the CausalODE benchmark, and AnnData export.
